    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In <i>Tower Offense</i>, an action-packed 1v1 tower defense/offense game, one player competes as a noble lord of the castle who defends his fortress with clever traps, archers and catapults - while the other is a ruthless besieger with knights, magicians and perhaps even dinosaurs who wants to bring the castle down. Who will win the duel for glory and conquest?</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Main Tower &amp; Objective</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The defender must protect his Main Tower - if it falls, the attacker wins.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Tower</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Defenders place towers on a grid to defend the <strong>Main Tower</strong>. Towers are available in three categories:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Offensive: Cause damage (e.g. archer tower, witch cauldron)</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Defensive: Block enemy units (e.g. walls)</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Resources: Increase income &amp; tower limits (e.g. mine, supply house)</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Units (Attacker)</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The attacker deploys units to destroy towers and reach the Main Tower. Each unit has its own strengths such as high damage, range or additional income.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Upgrade Tiers</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Both sides have 3 upgrade tiers:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Defender: Unlocks tiers with gold</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Attacker: Receives upgrades randomly via Card Upgrades</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Supply &amp; Income</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Supply: Determines how many towers &amp; units can be placed.</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Defender: Through supply houses</p></li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Attacker: Through card upgrades</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Income: Controls the gold per round.</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Defender: Through mines (+10 income per round)</p></li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Attackers: Through deployed units, dwarves or card upgrades</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Customizable Rounds</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Settings such as starting gold, supply &amp; number of rounds are customizable.</p>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In <i>Tower Offense</i>, an action-packed 1v1 tower defense/offense game, one player competes as a noble lord of the castle who defends his fortress with clever traps, archers and catapults - while the other is a ruthless besieger with knights, magicians and perhaps even dinosaurs who wants to bring the castle down. Who will win the duel for glory and conquest?</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Main Tower &amp; Objective</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The defender must protect his Main Tower - if it falls, the attacker wins.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Tower</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Defenders place towers on a grid to defend the <strong>Main Tower</strong>. Towers are available in three categories:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Offensive: Cause damage (e.g. archer tower, witch cauldron)</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Defensive: Block enemy units (e.g. walls)</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Resources: Increase income &amp; tower limits (e.g. mine, supply house)</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Units (Attacker)</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The attacker deploys units to destroy towers and reach the Main Tower. Each unit has its own strengths such as high damage, range or additional income.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Upgrade Tiers</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Both sides have 3 upgrade tiers:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Defender: Unlocks tiers with gold</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Attacker: Receives upgrades randomly via Card Upgrades</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Supply &amp; Income</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Supply: Determines how many towers &amp; units can be placed.</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Defender: Through supply houses</p></li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Attacker: Through card upgrades</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Income: Controls the gold per round.</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Defender: Through mines (+10 income per round)</p></li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Attackers: Through deployed units, dwarves or card upgrades</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Customizable Rounds</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Settings such as starting gold, supply &amp; number of rounds are customizable.</p>",
